<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to August 15.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>Rank Name			Price     pct change</p>
<p> 1   Oil Search		4.05     206.82</p>
<p> 2   Macquarie Bank	  13.35	93.48</p>
<p> 3   Hardie Inds		 4.73	71.30</p>
<p> 4   Fletcher-Energy div   4.75	70.48</p>
<p> 5   Wesfarmers		 13.01	66.79</p>
<p> 6   Sthn Pac Pete	     3.10	64.89</p>
<p> 7   Howard Smith	     13.40	59.52</p>
<p> 8   Natl Aust Bank	   19.21	58.24</p>
<p> 9   A N Z Bank		 10.25	57.45</p>
<p>10   Commonwealth Bk	  16.59	55.08</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>Rank Name				    Price     pct change</p>
<p> 1   Davids Limited	    0.85     -50.58</p>
<p> 2   Goldfields		  1.63     -44.75</p>
<p> 3   Newcrest Mining	   2.94     -39.88</p>
<p> 4   Sons Of Gwalia	    4.90     -39.51</p>
<p> 5   RGC			   3.70     -36.21</p>
<p> 6   Plutonic Rsc		3.92     -35.74</p>
<p> 7   Crown			 1.99     -30.43</p>
<p> 8   Great Central	     2.57     -28.61</p>
<p> 9   Normandy Min		1.61     -23.33</p>
<p>10   Village Roadshow	  4.38     -23.16</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
